# Prettier is no longer the repo's formatter. Biome owns every language it can parse --
# JS, TS, JSX, TSX, JSON, JSONC, CSS, GraphQL, HTML -- and Prettier is kept for exactly the
# two it cannot: Markdown and YAML. That is 67 .md and 23 .yaml/.yml files, including
# docs/adr/, the Kestra flows and the CI workflows, which would otherwise stop being
# format-checked entirely.
#
# The split is written HERE rather than as a glob in the `format` script because the
# Prettier CLI reads this file and nothing else. Handing one file to two formatters is how
# two definitions of "formatted" drift apart and the gate starts flapping.
*.ts
*.tsx
*.js
*.jsx
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.json
*.jsonc
*.css
*.html
*.graphql

node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
bun.lock
*.tsbuildinfo
specs/schema/
# Owned by release-please, which does not emit prettier-formatted markdown.
# Formatting it here would fight the release tooling and re-break every release.
CHANGELOG.md
# Owned by the Ymir wiki CLI, which writes and formats every page itself (`wiki fmt`) and
# validates them (`wiki check`). A PreToolUse hook blocks hand-edits for the same reason.
# Letting Prettier reformat them would put two formatters on one file -- the CHANGELOG.md
# argument above, with the added cost that a reformat can move a page's `[[link]]` lines
# and is not what `wiki validate` was run against.
wiki/
# Vendored, self-hosted webfont assets and their upstream licence/readme.
apps/ui/public/fonts/
# Untracked local tool state (gitignored too). Listed again because the Prettier CLI
# reads only this file, so without it `format:check` fails the gate on a developer's
# own scratch files -- and one of them is a dump of every live credential.
.dokploy.json
.dokploy-env.json
.kanna/
# Feature-branch worktrees, for the same reason: each is a second checkout of this repo, so
# Prettier would check every Markdown file in it again -- under whatever `.prettierignore`
# that branch happens to carry rather than this one.
.worktrees/
